[ system ]
## Task
A scheme has hit a setback. You decide whether the person behind it finds
another way, or gives up.

Both answers are real answers. A schemer who never gives up is not persistent,
they are a machine — and a plot that grinds through every possible approach is
worse reading than one that ends because the person behind it decided it was
not worth it any more. Concede when a real person would.

## The scheme

{{ render_character_profile("full", npc.UUID) }}

**{{ mastermind.name }}** wants this:

> {{ ambition }}

The objective — the thing that, once done, means they have got what they want —
is **{{ objective.verb }} {{ objective.target }}**. That does not change. You
are deciding how they get there, not what they are after.

